{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p232","rows":[{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preceding expression is accusative as the predicate of aṣbaḥa, or may be a circumstantial accusative; the adverb may serve as its predicate.","anchor":"منصوب على خبر أصبح وإن شئت على الحال ويكون الظرف في موضع الخبر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Moses was afraid someone would see him or discover him.","anchor":"قال الضحاك خاف أن يراه أحد أو يظهر عليه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["يترقب"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Yataraqqab means that Moses looked around repeatedly.","anchor":"قال و ( يترقب ) يتلفت","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["الذي استنصره بالأمس"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alladhī is nominative as the subject and yastaṣrikhu is its predicate; yastaṣrikhu may instead be a circumstantial clause.","anchor":"الذي في موضع رفع بالابتداء يستصرخه في موضع الخبر ويجوز أن يكون في موضع نصب على الحال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أكثر النحويين","stance":"reports","claim":"Most grammarians inflect ams when it has the definite article; some grammarians instead leave it indeclinable.","anchor":"أمس إذا دخلت عليه الألف واللام تمكن وأعرب عند أكثر النحويين ومنهم من يبنيه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"محمد بن يزيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Yazid says ams stays indeclinable because its definiteness differs from that of declinable nouns, and its final kasra resolves adjacent sukūns.","anchor":"العلة في بنائه عند محمد بن يزيد أن تعريفه ليس كتعريف المتمكنات فوجب أن يبنى ولا يعرب فكسر آخره","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Khalil explains the form ams as having lost its final yāʾ.","anchor":"ومذهب الخليل رحمه الله أن الياء محذوفة منه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الكوفيون","stance":"reports","claim":"One Kufan explanation derives ams by transfer from the expression ams bi-khayr.","anchor":"وللكوفيين فيه قولان أحدهما أنه منقول من قولهم أمس بخير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ gives the other Kufan explanation: the sīn's original vocalization is kasra.","anchor":"والآخر أن خلقة السين الكسر هذا قول الفراء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"سيبويه","stance":"reports","claim":"Sibawayh and others report a dialect that treats ams as a diptote in the nominative; poets sometimes extend that treatment to genitive and accusative, though nominative is the sounder usage.","anchor":"وحكى سيبويه وغيره أن من العرب من يجري أمس مجرى ما لا ينصرف في موضع الرفع خاصة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The cited poet uses the nominative-like form after the preposition mudh; the line witnesses this dialectal inflection of ams.","anchor":"لقد رأيت عجبا مذ أمسا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["أمس"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"When ams is indefinite or annexed, it is also declinable.","anchor":"وإذا أضيف أو نكر تمكن أيضا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:18"],"words":["لغوي مبين"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-ghawī means a frustrated loser, because the addressee confronts someone he cannot withstand.","anchor":"والغوي الخايب أي لأنك تشار من لا تطيقه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["أَن يَبْطِشَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The particle an is extra and serves emphasis.","anchor":"أن زائدة للتوكيد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["أَن يَبْطِشَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"يزيد بن القعقاع","stance":"reports","claim":"Yazīd ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ reads yabṭishu with ḍamma on its initial letter; this is an attested dialect, though yabṭisha is more familiar and ḍamma is more analogical for an intransitive verb.","anchor":"وقرأ يزيد بن القعقاع ( أن يبطش ) وهي لغة إلا أن ( يبطش ) أعرف منها وإن كان الضم أقيس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["جَبَّارًا فِي الْأَرْضِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima says a person is not a tyrant until he has killed two people.","anchor":"قال عكرمة لا يكون الإنسان جبارا حتى يقتل نفسين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["جَبَّارًا فِي الْأَرْضِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"holds","claim":"Abū Isḥāq defines a jabbar as an arrogant person who refuses to submit to God's command.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق الجبار في اللغة المتعظم الذي لا يخضع لأمر الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["جَبَّارًا فِي الْأَرْضِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"Ikrima's reading of the tyrant as a killer of two is compared with ʿAṭāʾ's warning that one must not assist, write for, or accompany an oppressor; he told a petitioner to discard his pen and seek God's provision.","anchor":"كما تأول عطاء فلن أكون ظهيرا للمجرمين على أنه لا يحل لأحد أن يعين ظالما","mentions":["28:17"]},{"verses":["28:19"],"words":["مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِينَ"],"type":"law","speaker":"عطاء","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAṭāʾ advised a petitioner not to help wrongdoers, including by writing for or accompanying them, and told him to throw away his pen and seek God's provision.","anchor":"حتى قال لمن استفتاه ارم قلمك واسترزق الله جل وعز ولا تكن ظهيرا للمجرمين","mentions":["28:17"]},{"verses":["28:22"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"holds","claim":"Moses took the road leading toward Midian; sawāʾ al-sabīl means the straight or direct road.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق أي سلك الطريق الذي هو تلقاء مدين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:22"],"words":["مدين"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq says Midian does not decline because it is a place name.","anchor":"ولم ينصرف مدين لأنه اسم للبقعة","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p242","rows":[{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["قَارُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Qārūn is a foreign proper name and is indeclinable; foreign names on the fāʿūl pattern that do not take al are declined as indefinite, while suitable masculine names with al, such as Ṭāwūs and Rāqūd, are declinable.","anchor":"إن قارون لم ينصرف لأنه اسم أعجمي وما كان على فاعول أعجميا لا يحسن فيه الألف واللام لم ينصرف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["قَارُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq says Qārūn would be declinable if it were Arabic, derived from qarantu al-shayʾ.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق ولو كان قارون من العربية من قرنت الشيء لانصرف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مَا إِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"An with its subject forms the relative complement of mā.","anchor":"أن واسمها في صلة ما","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مَا إِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"علي بن سليمان","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿAlī ibn Sulaymān rejects the Kufans' claim that an cannot form the complement of a relative pronoun, pointing to this Qur'anic construction.","anchor":"وسمعت علي بن سليمان يقول ما أقبح ما يقول الكوفيون في الصلاة أنه لا يجوز","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["مَفَاتِحَهُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mafātiḥ is the plural of maftaḥ; whoever uses miftāḥ instead has the plural mafātīḥ.","anchor":"وهو جمع مفتح ومن قال مفتاح قال مفاتيح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوءُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"prefers","claim":"The best explanation is that the keys make the group lean under their weight, as in expressions where one causes another to go or come.","anchor":"أحسن ما قيل فيه أن المعنى لتنيء العصبة أي تميلهم من ثقلها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَتَنُوءُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In the paired idiom mā sāʾahu wa-nāʾahu, nāʾahu is a follow-on to sāʾahu; the expected form would be anāʾahu, as in hanāʾanī wa-marāʾanī and mā qaddama wa-mā ḥadatha.","anchor":"فأما قولهم له عندي ما ساءه وناءه فهو اتباع كان يجب أن يقال وأناءه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِذْ قَالَ لَهُ قَوْمُهُ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ says Moses alone addressed Qārūn, using a plural expression, as in the report that people spoke to the believers when the speaker was one man, Nuʿaym ibn Masʿūd.","anchor":"تأوله الفراء على أن موسى صلى الله عليه وسلم هو الذي قاله له وحده فجمع ومثله","mentions":["3:173"]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["إِذْ قَالَ لَهُ قَوْمُهُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"علي بن سليمان","stance":"rejects","claim":"ʿAlī ibn Sulaymān rejects al-Farrāʾ's singular-speaker analysis as defeating the clarity of the statement; Nuʿaym and those who followed him were the speakers.","anchor":"وسمعت علي بن سليمان يقول غير هذا وينكر ما قال الفراء لأنه بطلان البيان","mentions":["3:173"]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["لَا تَفْرَحْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"holds","claim":"Do not exult in wealth, since such joy results in failing to give wealth its due.","anchor":"تأوله أبو إسحاق على أن المعنى لا تفرح بالمال لأن الفرح لا يؤدي فيه الحق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["الْفَرِحِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ distinguishes farḥīn as people currently in joy from fāriḥīn as people who will rejoice later, comparing ṭamiʿ and ṭāmiʿ and mayyit and māʾit.","anchor":"فرق الفراء بين الفرحين والفارحين وزعم أن الفرحين الذين هم في حال الفرح","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:76"],"words":["الْفَرِحِينَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"The distinction al-Farrāʾ draws is contradicted by 69:21, which says mayyit rather than māʾit for those who are dead.","anchor":"وبذلك على خلاف ما قال قول الله جل وعز ﴿ إنك ميت وإنهم ميتون ﴾ ولم يقل مائت","mentions":["69:21"]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ gives two senses: Qārūn claims the wealth on the basis of merit he possesses, or of knowledge as he understands it.","anchor":"تأوله الفراء على معنيين أحدهما على فضل عندي والآخر على علم فيما رأى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"holds","claim":"Abū Isḥāq understands Qārūn to mean he acquired the wealth through knowledge of the Torah, which he knew.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق المعنى إنما أوتيته على علم بالتوراة لأنه كان عالما بها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["28:78"],"words":["عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"rejects","claim":"Abū Isḥāq rejects the claim that Qārūn practiced alchemy, since alchemy is false and has no reality.","anchor":"وأنكر قول من قال إنه كان يعمل الكيمياء قال لأن الكيمياء باطل لا حقيقة له","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p252","rows":[{"verses":["29:15"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الكسائي","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Kisāʾī parses the preceding noun as coordinated with the object suffix pronoun.","anchor":"معطوف على الهاء قال الكسائي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:16"],"words":["وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ibrāhīm is accusative, coordinated with the object pronoun in the preceding verb.","anchor":"منصوب بأنجينا بعني أنه معطوف على الهاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:16"],"words":["وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A second possible parse coordinates Ibrāhīm with Noah, giving the sense We sent Ibrāhīm.","anchor":"وأجاز أن يكون معطوفا على نوح والمعنى وأرسلنا إبراهيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:16"],"words":["وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A third possible parse makes Ibrāhīm accusative under an implied command: Remember Ibrāhīm.","anchor":"وقول ثالث أن يكون منصوبا بمعنى واذكر إبراهيم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:17"],"words":["إِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In innamā, mā is a particle that blocks inna; it cannot be a relative complement because inna does not govern a verb.","anchor":"ما كافة ولا يجوز أن يكون صلة لأن إن لا تقع على الفعل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:17"],"words":["إِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Even when a noun follows, as in innamā Zaydun jālis, mā remains a blocking particle.","anchor":"فإن كان بعد ما اسم فقلت إنما زيد جالس فما أيضا كافة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:17"],"words":["إِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"بعض النحويين","stance":"reports","claim":"Some grammarians allow mā to be a relative pronoun, as in innamā Zaydan jālis.","anchor":"وأجاز بعض النحويين أن يكون صلة فتقول إنما زيدا جالس","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:17"],"words":["أَوْثَانًا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Outside the Qur'anic reading, awthānan may be nominative if mā is a relative pronoun, taʿbudūna its clause with an omitted pronoun, and awthānan the predicate of inna.","anchor":"ويجوز في غير القرآن رفع أوثان","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:17"],"words":["وَتَخْلُقُونَ إِفْكًا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ifkan is accusative as the direct object of the verb alone.","anchor":"فأما ( وتخلقون إفكا ) فهو منصوب بالفعل لا غير","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p254","rows":[{"verses":["29:27"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preceding construction has two objects; its details were explained elsewhere.","anchor":"مفعولان قال أبو جعفر قد ذكرناه وبينا معناه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:27"],"words":["فِي الْآخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Fī al-ākhirah is parenthetical clarification, not part of the relative clause.","anchor":"ليس في الآخرة داخلا في الصلة وإنما هو تبيين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:28"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الكسائي","stance":"prefers","claim":"Al-Kisāʾī prefers understanding the clause as We sent Lot, though he also allows We saved Lot.","anchor":"قال الكسائي المعنى وأنجينا لوطا أو أرسلنا لوطا قال وهذا الوجه أحب إلي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:29"],"words":["أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"قراءة الكوفيين","stance":"reports","claim":"The Kufan reading interrogates the first and second occurrences; Abū ʿAmr does likewise but lightens the hamza.","anchor":"في الأولى والثانية على الاستفهام وكذا قراءة أبي عمرو إلا أنه يخفف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:29"],"words":["أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ","وَتَأْتُونَ فِي نَادِيكُمُ الْمُنكَرَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"نافع","stance":"reports","claim":"Nāfiʿ reads the first occurrence without interrogation and interrogates the second; this follows the written form and is an emphatic challenge rather than a question.","anchor":"وقرأ نافع ( إنكم ) بغير استفهام في الأولى واستفهم في الثانية وهذه القراءة على اتباع السواد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:29"],"words":["أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"محمد بن يزيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Muḥammad ibn Yazīd compares this emphatic, non-interrogative reading with the poet's exchange: they asked whether he loved her, and he answered certainly.","anchor":"وكذا قال محمد بن يزيد في قول الشاعر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:29"],"words":["أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو عبيد","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿUbayd considers the first reading remote because it places two interrogatives together.","anchor":"القراءة الأولى عند أبي عبيد بعيدة للجمع بين الاستفهامين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["29:29"],"words":["أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"The author rejects Abū ʿUbayd's objection: a question may follow a question, and the comparison he cites from this sūra is unlike this construction.","anchor":"قال أبو جعفر وليس الأمر كذلك لأن هذا استفهام بعد استفهام وليس ينكر في مثل هذا استفهامان","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p265","rows":[{"verses":["30:6"],"words":["وَعْدَ اللَّهِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq parses waʿda Allāh as an emphatic verbal noun and allows nominative waʿdu Allāh to mean This is God's promise.","anchor":"مصدر مؤكد قال أبو إسحاق ويجوز","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:6"],"words":["أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The people who do not know are the disbelievers, who constitute the majority.","anchor":"وهم الكفار وهم أكثر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:7"],"words":["وَهُم عَنِ الْآخِرَةِ هُمْ غَافِلُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"On one parse, the first hum is the subject, the second begins a new clause whose predicate is the rest, and that clause predicates the first; the repetition emphasizes the statement.","anchor":"هم الأول ابتداء والثاني ابتداء ثان والجملة خبر الأول وفي الكلام معنى التوكيد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:7"],"words":["وَهُم عَنِ الْآخِرَةِ هُمْ غَافِلُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Alternatively, the second hum is an emphatic apposition to the first.","anchor":"ويجوز أن يكون هم الثاني بدلا من الأول كما تقول رأيته إياه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:8"],"words":["بِلِقَاءِ رَبِّهِمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The emphatic lām is brought forward in a reordered construction; the author explains its placement with examples showing it may precede a predicate phrase but not follow both the subject and predicate.","anchor":"اللام للتوكيد والتقدير لكافرون بلقاء ربهم على التقديم والتأخير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:9"],"words":["*"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Meccans were not people accustomed to warfare.","anchor":"لأن أهل مكة لم يكونوا أصحاب حرب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:10"],"words":["السُّوأَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Kāna is feminine because its subject's femininity is nonliteral; al-sūʾā is its predicate, but those who put ʿāqibata in the accusative take al-sūʾā as the subject.","anchor":"اسم كان وذكرت لأن تأنيثها غير حقيقي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:10"],"words":["السُّوأَىٰ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الأعمش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Aʿmash reads the ending with al-sūʾ raised; an kadhdhabū is accusative with the sense because they denied.","anchor":"وروي عن الأعمش أنه قرأ","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:12"],"words":["يُبْلِسُ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"أبو عبد الرحمن السلمي","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī reads yublisu with fatḥa on the lām.","anchor":"وقرأ أبو عبد الرحمن السلمي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:12"],"words":["يُبْلِسُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"In ordinary usage, ablasa describes a man falling silent, losing his argument, and having no hope of producing one; it is close to becoming bewildered.","anchor":"والمعروف في اللغة أبلس الرجل إذا سكت وانقطعت حجته ولم يؤمل أن تكون له حجة وقريب منه تحير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:12"],"words":["يُبْلِسُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The rajaz line قال نعم أعرفه وأبلسا cites the word ablasa for falling silent.","anchor":"قال الراجز ( قال نعم أعرفه وأبلسا )","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:12"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"بعض النحويين","stance":"reports","claim":"Some grammarians derive the name Iblīs from ablasa, meaning his argument was cut off.","anchor":"وقد زعم بعض النحويين أن إبليس مشتق من هذا وأنه أبلس أي انقطعت حجته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:12"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"rejects","claim":"The proposed derivation would require Iblīs to be declinable, whereas the Qur'anic name is indeclinable; the claim that it is uniquely weighty because no one else bore it does not resolve the issue.","anchor":"ولو كان كما قال لوجب أن ينصرف وهو في القرآن غير منصرف فاحتج بعضهم بأنه اسم ثقل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:13"],"words":["بِشُرَكَائِهِمْ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their partners are the beings they worshipped apart from God; on the Day of Resurrection they will disown them as gods.","anchor":"قيل يعني بشركائهم ما عبدوه من دون الله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:15"],"words":["فَأَمَّا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq explains ammā as leaving the current subject and taking up another; Sibawayh explains it as whatever the case may be, then turning to another matter.","anchor":"سمعت أبا إسحاق يقول معنى أما دع ما كنا فيه وخذ في غيره وكذا قال سيبويه إن معناها مهما يكن من شيء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:15"],"words":["الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا فَهُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Alladhīna is a nominative subject; hum begins a second nominal clause, which is predicated of the first subject.","anchor":"( الذين آمنوا ) في موضع رفع بالابتداء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:15"],"words":["فِي رَوْضَةٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الضحاك","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk says fī rawḍa means in a garden; riyāḍ is the plural for gardens.","anchor":"قال الضحاك ( في روضة ) في جنة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:15"],"words":["فِي رَوْضَةٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو عبيدة","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū ʿUbayda says a rawḍa is in a low-lying place; if elevated, it is called a turʿa.","anchor":"وقال أبو عبيدة الروضة ما كان في تسفل فإن كان مرتفعا فهو ترعة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["30:15"],"words":["فِي رَوْضَةٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another scholar says a garden is at its best on high, rugged ground, and cites a line by al-Aʿshā.","anchor":"وقال غيره أحسن ما تكون الروضة إذا كانت في موضع مرتفع غليظ كما قال الأعشى","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p293","rows":[{"verses":["32:11"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq explains yatawaffākum as completing and taking the full number of you all.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق هو من توفيه العدد أي يستوفي عددكم أجمعين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:12"],"words":["لَوْ تَرَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause is parsed as a nominal sentence with subject and predicate.","anchor":"مبتدأ وخبر قال أبو إسحاق المخاطبة للنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مخاطبة لأمته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:12"],"words":["لَوْ تَرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq says the singular address to the Prophet speaks to the community, with the sense If you all were to see.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق المخاطبة للنبي صلى الله عليه وسلم مخاطبة لأمته والمعنى ولو ترون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:12"],"words":["لَوْ تَرَىٰ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو العباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū al-ʿAbbās instead takes the address directly to Muḥammad: if he saw the criminals, he would regret his earlier course; the response to law is omitted.","anchor":"ومذهب أبي العباس غير هذا وأن يكون المعنى يا محمد قل للمجرم ولو ترى إذ المجرمون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:13"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preceding construction has two objects.","anchor":"مفعولان قيل في معناه قولان أحدهما أن سياق الكلام يدل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:13"],"words":["وَلَٰكِنْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ مِنِّي"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"One explanation reads the context as the afterlife: had God willed, He would have returned them to worldly testing as they asked, but His decree is to punish the disobedient in Hell; He knew they would relapse if returned, as 6:28 says.","anchor":"أي لو شئنا لرددناهم إلى الدنيا والمحنة كما سألوا","mentions":["6:28"]},{"verses":["32:14"],"words":["نَسِينَاكُمْ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One explanation takes forgetting literally: they failed to remember to prepare for this Day and were like forgetters.","anchor":"أحدهما أنه من النسيان الذي لا ذكر معه أي لم تعملوا لهذا اليوم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:14"],"words":["نَسِينَاكُمْ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"محمد بن يزيد","stance":"prefers","claim":"A second explanation takes nasīnā as abandoned; Ibn Yazīd argues from Adam's failure to keep God's command, not a lapse of memory, since Satan had told him what God forbade.","anchor":"واحتج محمد بن يزيد بقوله","mentions":["20:115"]},{"verses":["32:14"],"words":["نَسِينَاكُمْ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The cited verse about a skewer left in a side demonstrates that nasūhu can mean they left or abandoned it.","anchor":"سفود شرب نسوه عند مفتأد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:15"],"words":["الَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِّرُوا بِهَا"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Those who believe in God's signs, proofs, and evidences are the ones who humble themselves to Him and glorify Him when reminded.","anchor":"أي إنما يؤمن بالعلاقات والبراهين والحجج الذين إذا ذكروا بها خضعوا لله","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:15"],"words":["وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"They are not too proud to worship God or submit to what He has made clear.","anchor":"عن عبادته ولا الانقياد لما أبانه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:16"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preceding verb may be accusative as a circumstantial clause or nominative; its inflection is not visible because it is maqṣūr, whose inflection is suppressed, unlike manqūṣ, whose inflection is reduced.","anchor":"في موضع نصب على الحال أو رفع لأنه فعل مستقبل ولم يتبين فيه الإعراب لأنه فعل مقصور","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:16"],"words":["يَدْعُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Yadʿūna is an accusative circumstantial clause.","anchor":"في موضع نصب على الحال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:16"],"words":["خَوْفًا وَطَمَعًا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Khawfan is a purpose accusative or a verbal noun; ṭamaʿan has the same parse, meaning fear of punishment and hope for reward.","anchor":"مفعول من أجله ويجوز أن يكون مصدرا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:16"],"words":["مِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنْفِقُونَ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mā may be a relative pronoun or a verbal noun; on either analysis it is written separately from min.","anchor":"تكون ما بمعنى الذي وتكون مصدرا وفي كلا الوجهين يجب أن تكون منفصلة من من","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p295","rows":[{"verses":["32:17"],"words":["مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُم"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A reading with sukūn on the yāʾ makes ukhfiya a future verb; ʿAbd Allāh reads nakhfī with nūn, and Abū Isḥāq also gives the sense what God has hidden for them.","anchor":"ويقرأ ( ما أخفي لهم ) بإسكان الياء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:17"],"words":["مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"holds","claim":"If mā is relative, it is accusative in all readings; if it means ayy, it is nominative in the Medinan reading and accusative in the others.","anchor":"فإن جعلت ما بمعنى الذي كانت في موضع نصب على الوجوه كلها وإن جعلتها بمعنى أي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:17"],"words":["جَزَاءً"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Jazāʾan is a purpose accusative or a verbal noun.","anchor":"مفعول من أجله أو مصدر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:18"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"كثير من النحويين","stance":"reports","claim":"Many grammarians explain the plural verb by saying man conveys a group.","anchor":"لأن لفظ من تؤدى عن الجماعة فلهذا قال لا يستوون هذا قول كثير من النحويين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:18"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"بعض النحويين","stance":"reports","claim":"Other grammarians say the verb refers to two people, since a pair counts as a plural formed by joining one to another.","anchor":"وقال بعضهم يستوون لاثنين إلا أن الاثنين جمع لأنه واحد جمع مع آخر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:18"],"words":["أَفَمَن كَانَ مُؤْمِنًا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"A report from Ibn ʿAbbās and others says the verse was revealed about ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, the believer, and al-Walīd ibn ʿUqba ibn Abī Muʿayṭ, the sinner; the report supports the dual referent reading.","anchor":"والحديث يدل على هذا القول لأنه عن ابن عباس رحمه الله وغيره قال نزلت أفمن كان مؤمنا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:19"],"words":["فَلَهُمْ جَنَّاتُ الْمَأْوَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Man is nominative as the subject, described as a believer; the predicate begins with fa-lahum jannāt al-maʾwā, plural because it means he and those like him.","anchor":"في موضع رفع بالابتداء فوصفه الله جل وعز بالإيمان وخبر الابتداء ( فلهم جنات المأوى )","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:20"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase in verse 32:20 is parsed as an adverbial expression.","anchor":"وكذا\\n20\\nظرف\\n21\\nلام قسم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:21"],"words":["لَنُذِيقَنَّهُم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The lām is an oath particle.","anchor":"20\\nظرف\\n21\\nلام قسم ( من العذاب الأدنى )","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:21"],"words":["الْعَذَابِ الْأَدْنَىٰ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-adnā means the nearer punishment; most exegetes identify it as worldly afflictions.","anchor":"أي الأقرب وأكثر أهل التفسير على أنها المصيبات في الدنيا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:22"],"words":["مِمَّن ذُكِّرَ بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The person who turns away after being reminded of God's proofs and signs wrongs himself; aʿraḍa means to reject them, after which God says He will take vengeance on the guilty.","anchor":"أي لنفسه ممن ذكر بآيات ربه أي بحججه وعلاماته","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:23"],"words":["فَلَا تَكُن فِي مِرْيَةٍ مِّن لِّقَائِهِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preceding construction has two objects; the detailed analysis was given elsewhere.","anchor":"مفعولان ( فلا تكن في مرية من لقائه ) قد ذكرناه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:23"],"words":["مِن لِّقَائِهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One reported explanation takes the phrase as reassurance that Moses received the Book willingly.","anchor":"وقد قيل إن معناه فلا تكن في شك من تلقي موسى صلى الله عليه وسلم الكتاب بالقبول","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:23"],"words":["فَلَا تَكُن فِي مِرْيَةٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan says Moses received the Book but was harmed and denied; the Prophet should not doubt that he too will face denial and harm. The source calls this unusual and says it is transmitted by ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd.","anchor":"وعن الحسن أنه قال في معناه ولقد آتينا موسى الكتاب فأوذي وكذب فلا تكن في شك","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:24"],"words":["أَئِمَّةً"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الكوفيون","stance":"reports","claim":"The Kufans read the word as a form with two hamzas in one word; all grammarians call it an error, since such a combination is impermissible except with easing in Ādam and ākhir.","anchor":"والكوفيون يقرؤون ( أمة ) وهو لحن عند جميع النحويين لأنه جمع بين همزتين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:24"],"words":["أَئِمَّةً"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The underlying form is aʾimmima; the first mīm's vowel moves to the hamza, the mīms assimilate, and the second hamza is lightened to avoid adjacent hamzas.","anchor":"الأصل أأممة ثم ألقيت حركة الميم الأولى على الهمزة وأدغمت الميم في الميم وخففت الهمزة الثانية","mentions":[]},{"verses":["32:24"],"words":["لَمَّا صَبَرُوا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Lammā ṣabarū can mean because they were patient or when they were patient; God made them leaders for their patience.","anchor":"لصبرهم و ( لما صبروا ) أي حين صبروا جعلناهم أئمة","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p302","rows":[{"verses":["33:5"],"words":["فَإِخْوَانُكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَمَوَالِيكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Those whose fathers are unknown are your brothers in religion and your clients; mawālī is coordinated with ikhwa.","anchor":"أي فهم إخوانكم ( ومواليكم )","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:5"],"words":["فِيمَا أَخْطَأْتُم بِهِ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda explains error as attributing a man to someone other than his father while believing that person really is his father.","anchor":"قول قتادة هو أن ينسب الرجل إلى غير أبيه وهو يرى أنه أبوه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:5"],"words":["فِيمَا أَخْطَأْتُم بِهِ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another explanation generalizes the exemption to anything done by mistake; ʿAṭāʾ ruled that someone who unknowingly takes glass for payment or greets an unrecognized person does not incur liability or break an oath.","anchor":"وقد قيل إن هذا مجمل أي وليس عليكم جناح في شيء أخطأتم به وكانت فتيا عطاء على هذا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:5"],"words":["مَا تَعَمَّدَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mā may be genitive, coordinated with the mā governed by bi in the preceding phrase, or nominative after an implied subject: what you are held accountable for is what your hearts intended.","anchor":"ما في موضع خفض ردا على ما التي مع أخطأتم ويجوز أن يكون في موضع رفع على إضمار مبتدأ","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["النَّبِيُّ أَوْلَىٰ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One explanation makes the Prophet more entitled to believers than they are to one another, with anfus meaning fellow believers as in 2:54.","anchor":"أحدهما النبي أولى بالمؤمنين من بعضهم لبعض","mentions":["2:54"]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["النَّبِيُّ أَوْلَىٰ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"Another explanation says the Prophet's command takes precedence whenever personal desire draws a believer elsewhere.","anchor":"والآخر أنه إذا أمر النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بشيء ودعت النفس إلى غيره كان أمر النبي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["النَّبِيُّ أَوْلَىٰ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"A prophetic report says he has greater claim over believers than their own selves; property goes to heirs, while debt and dependents are his responsibility.","anchor":"وفي الحديث أنا أولى بالمؤمنين من أنفسهم من ترك مالا فلورثته ومن ترك دينا أو ضياعا فعلي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["وَأَزْوَاجُهُ أُمَّهَاتُهُمْ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Prophet's wives are mothers in respect of sanctity, and believers may not marry them.","anchor":"أي في الحرمة ولا يحل لهم تزوجهن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["وَأُولُو الْأَرْحَامِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ulū al-arḥām may be the subject, with baʿḍuhum a second subject or an appositive.","anchor":"مبتدأ و ( بعضهم ) مبتدأ ثان أو بدل","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["أَوْلَىٰ بِبَعْضٍ فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The phrase can mean that kin are closer than the believers and emigrants, or that kin among the believers and emigrants are closer to one another.","anchor":"يكون التقدير وأولوا الأرحام من المؤمنين والمهاجرين ويجوز أن يكون المعنى أولى من المؤمنين","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["إِلَّا أَن تَفْعَلُوا إِلَىٰ أَوْلِيَائِكُم مَّعْرُوفًا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The exception is accusative and is not an exception from the preceding class.","anchor":"في موضع نصب استثناء ليس من الأول","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["إِلَّا أَن تَفْعَلُوا إِلَىٰ أَوْلِيَائِكُم مَّعْرُوفًا"],"type":"law","speaker":"محمد بن الحنفية","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn al-Ḥanafiyya says the verse was revealed to permit bequests to Jewish and Christian relatives.","anchor":"قال محمد بن الحنفية رحمة الله عليه نزلت في إجازة الوصية لليهودي والنصراني","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:6"],"words":["مَسْطُورًا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mastūran means written in a row like a line; the plurals of saṭr are asṭār and sutūr, with the form beginning with a still consonant more common.","anchor":"أي مكتوبا في نسق كالسطر ويقال سطر والجمع أسطار","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:7"],"words":["مِيثَاقَهُمْ"],"type":"reports","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās, through the chain cited from al-Thawrī, Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, says the covenant was taken from the prophets on behalf of their peoples.","anchor":"قال الثوري عن حبيب بن أبي ثابت عن سعيد بن جبير عن ابن عباس وإذ أخذنا من النبيين ميثاقهم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:7"],"words":["*"],"type":"reports","speaker":"أبي بن كعب","stance":"reports","claim":"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb compares this covenant with 7:172: the prophets' covenant was taken with prophetic light in them like lamps, then a specific covenant of the prophetic mission was taken from the prophets.","anchor":"وعن أبي بن كعب قال هو مثل","mentions":["7:172"]},{"verses":["33:7"],"words":["وَمِن نُّوحٍ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preposition is repeated before Noah because an overt noun coordinated with a declined pronoun repeats its preposition, as in marartu bihi wa-bi-Zayd.","anchor":"ومن نوح ولم يقل ونوح لأن المظهر إذا عطف على المضمر المخفوض أعيد الحرف","mentions":[]},{"verses":["33:7"],"words":["وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ وَمُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The preposition is not repeated before Ibrāhīm because it is coordinated with the overt noun Noah; likewise Mūsā and ʿĪsā are coordinated with overt nouns.","anchor":"عطف مظهر على مظهر فلم يعد الحرف وكذا ( وموسى وعيسى )","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p345","rows":[{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["أَذِنَ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The forms adhina and udhina carry the same meaning.","anchor":"أذن وأذن بمعنى واحد كما مر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["إِلَّا لِمَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"The man allowed to benefit may refer either to the intercessors or to those for whom intercession is made.","anchor":"من ههنا للشافعين ويجوز أن تكون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["إِلَّا لِمَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُ"],"type":"referent","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"prefers","claim":"Abū Isḥāq prefers the intercessors as referent because the following clause about fear being removed concerns the angels.","anchor":"وزعم أبو إسحاق أنها للشافعين أشبه بالمعنى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"قراءة العامة","stance":"reports","claim":"The common reading has fuzziʿa; its sense, shared with the open-vowel variant, is that God removed fear from the hearts.","anchor":"وفي هذا خمس قراءات قراءة العامة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"ابن مسعود","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn Masʿūd, Ibn ʿAbbās, Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, and Mujāhid read with fatḥa on fāʾ and zāy; it has the same meaning as the common reading.","anchor":"وعن ابن مسعود وابن عباس وسعيد بن جبير ومجاهد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan is reported to read faraġa with a ḍamma on fāʾ and unpointed rāʾ followed by ghayn; Abū Mujliz reads the same form.","anchor":"وروى هيثم عن عوف عن الحسن أنه قرأ","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan is also reported through Maṭar al-Warrāq to read fuzziʿa with ḍamma on the fāʾ.","anchor":"وروى مطر الوراق عن الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الحسن","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Ḥasan is reported through Ayyūb and Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl to read faraġa with ḍamma on fāʾ and a light, unpointed rāʾ followed by ghayn; al-Naḥḥās calls all these chains sound and unobjectionable.","anchor":"وروى أيوب وحميد الطويل عن الحسن","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَن قُلُوبِهِمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"مجاهد","stance":"reports","claim":"Mujāhid locates this scene on the Day of Resurrection, when the covering is lifted.","anchor":"إلا أن مجاهدا قال في تفسير هذه الآية على ما رواه عنه ورقاء عن أبي نجيح إنها في يوم القيامة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["قَالُوا مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Mādhā is accusative as the object of qāl; alternatively, mā is a subject and dhā its predicate, with the sense that which.","anchor":"ماذا في موضع نصب بقال","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["قَالُوا الْحَقَّ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-ḥaqq may be accusative when mādhā is accusative, or nominative when mā is nominative.","anchor":"على أن ماذا في موضع نصب أي قال الحق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["الْعَلِيُّ الْكَبِيرُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Huwa al-ʿaliyy al-kabīr is a subject and predicate construction.","anchor":"ابتداء وخبر و العلي الجبار المتعالي","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:23"],"words":["الْعَلِيُّ الْكَبِيرُ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Al-ʿali means the overpowering, exalted one; al-kabīr means the master who is sought.","anchor":"الجبار المتعالي و الكبير السيد المقصود","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["مَن يَرْزُقُكُم"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Man is a complete interrogative noun in the nominative as subject, and yarzuqukum is its predicate.","anchor":"من في موضع رفع بالابتداء وهي اسم تام لأنها للاستفهام","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["يَرْزُقُكُم"],"type":"readings","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The qāf may assimilate into the kāf, changing the qāf into a kāf.","anchor":"ويجوز إدغام القاف في الكاف فتقلب القاف كافا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["وَإِنَّا"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Innā is shortened from innana by deleting one nūn.","anchor":"والأصل وإننا فحذفت النون تخفيفا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["أَوْ إِيَّاكُمْ لَعَلَىٰ هُدًى أَوْ فِي ضَلَالٍ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Iyyākum is coordinated with the subject of inna; coordination by syntactic position would instead use antum and would make guidance apply only to the first group.","anchor":"معطوف على اسم إن ولو عطف على الموضع لكان أو أنتم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["أَوْ إِيَّاكُمْ لَعَلَىٰ هُدًى"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"أبو العباس","stance":"prefers","claim":"Abū al-ʿAbbās allows the guidance phrase to apply to the first group; the wording rhetorically presses an opponent to see that one side must be right and the other mistaken.","anchor":"ويجوز أن يكون للأول وهو اختيار أبي العباس قال ومعناه معنى قول المستنصر بصاحبه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["34:24"],"words":["*"],"type":"rhetoric","speaker":"أبو العباس","stance":"holds","claim":"The construction resembles saying I will do one thing and you another, and one of us is mistaken, while leaving the listener to recognize which one.","anchor":"أحدنا كاذب وقد عرف المعنى وكما تقول أنا أفعل كذا وتفعل أنت كذا","mentions":[]}]}
{"loc":"NAHHAS:v3p367","rows":[{"verses":["35:12"],"words":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The cited poetic line uses the word al-mufāyil in describing a ship's prow cleaving water, as evidence for the preceding lexical discussion.","anchor":"يشق حباب الماء حيزومها بها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:13"],"words":["لِأَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"reports","claim":"One view identifies the appointed term as the Resurrection, since God has assigned it a known time.","anchor":"وقيل الأجل المسمى ههنا القيامة لأنها عند الله جل وعز مسماة لوقت معلوم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:13"],"words":["قِطْمِيرٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"ابن عباس","stance":"reports","claim":"Ibn ʿAbbās, through ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥa, says qitmir is the thin skin around a date pit.","anchor":"قال علي بن أبي طلحة عن ابن عباس القطمير جلد النواة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:14"],"words":["إِن تَدْعُوهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوا دُعَاءَكُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause is conditional with its result; the following law clause carries the sense of the first even though law is not normally used for a conditional result.","anchor":"فيه معنى الأول وإن كانت لولا يجازى بها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:14"],"words":["وَلَوْ سَمِعُوا مَا اسْتَجَابُوا لَكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda explains their failure to respond as their not following or accepting the callers.","anchor":"قال قتادة ما استجابوا لكم ما تبعوكم ولا قبلوا منكم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:14"],"words":["وَيَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ يَكْفُرُونَ بِشِرْكِكُمْ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"أبو إسحاق","stance":"reports","claim":"Abū Isḥāq says the false gods will say that their worshippers were not worshipping them.","anchor":"قال أبو إسحاق أي يقولون ما كانوا إيانا يعبدون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:14"],"words":["وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثْلُ خَبِيرٍ"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"قتادة","stance":"reports","claim":"Qatāda says God has informed people that this disavowal will occur on the Day of Resurrection.","anchor":"قال قتادة الله جل وعز أخبر أنه يكون هذا منكم يوم القيامة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:15"],"words":["يَٰٓأَيُّهَا النَّاسُ أَنتُمُ الْفُقَرَاءُ"],"type":"readings","speaker":"الخليل","stance":"prefers","claim":"Al-Khalīl considers easing the second hamza in al-fuqarāʾ the best option; also permitted are easing or dropping the first, easing both, or pronouncing both clearly.","anchor":"بتخفيف الهمزة الثانية أجود الوجوه عند الخليل رحمه الله ويجوز تخفيف الأولى وحذفها","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:15"],"words":["وَاللَّهُ هُوَ الْغَنِيُّ الْحَمِيدُ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Huwa may be an extra particle without a syntactic position or a nominative subject.","anchor":"تكون هو زائدة فلا يكون لها موضع من الإعراب وتكون مبتدأ فيكون موضعها رفعا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:16"],"words":["إِن يَشَأْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This is a conditional construction with ellipsis commonly used in Arabic: if He wills to remove you, He removes you; the verb's ḍamma is deleted, then the preceding alif drops when the hamza becomes still.","anchor":"شرط ومجازاة وفيه حذف تستعمله العرب كثيرا والتقدير إن يشأ أن يذهبكم يذهبكم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:16"],"words":["وَيَأْتِ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Yaʾti is coordinated with yudhhibkum.","anchor":"( ويأت ) معطوف على يذهبكم","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This clause is detached from what precedes; the original form had an initial wāw, deleted to match yaziru.","anchor":"مقطوع مما قبله والأصل توزر حذفت الواو اتباعا ليزر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَازِرَةٌ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Wāziran is an adjective for an omitted noun meaning a burden-bearing soul.","anchor":"( وازرة ) نعت لمحذوف أي نفس وازرة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ supplies an omitted nafs or dābba; the expression can apply to masculine or feminine.","anchor":"قال الفراء أي نفس مثقلة أو دابة قال وهذا يقع للمذكر والمؤنث","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash supplies an omitted human being: if a burdened person calls another person.","anchor":"قال الأخفش أي وإن تدع مثقلة إنسانا","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Ḥaml is a load carried on the back; al-Kisāʾī gives fatḥa alone for a woman's pregnancy and a palm's fruit, while Ibn al-Sikkīt allows either fatḥa or kasra for palm fruit.","anchor":"والحمل ما كان على الظهر وحمل المرأة وحمل النخلة حكاهما الكسائي بالفتح لا غير","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الأخفش","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Akhfash supplies the omitted word al-insān: even if the person called were a close relative.","anchor":"التقدير على قول الأخفش ولو كان الإنسان المدعو ذا قربى","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"الفراء","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Farrāʾ also permits the nominative form dhū qurba.","anchor":"وأجاز الفراء ( ولو كان ذو قربى )","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبَىٰ"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The nominative construction is valid according to Sibawayh, as in wa-in kāna dhū ʿusra; kāna may mean occurred or have an omitted predicate, and Sibawayh's example about people being repaid good for good illustrates the two analyses.","anchor":"قال أبو جعفر وهذا جائز عند سيبويه ومثله","mentions":["65:7"]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["وَإِن تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ إِلَىٰ حِمْلِهَا"],"type":"reports","speaker":"عكرمة","stance":"reports","claim":"ʿIkrima reports that a Jew or Christian may ask a Muslim on Judgment Day to repay a past kindness by taking some punishment or a sin; the Muslim refuses from fear, as do fathers, sons, and spouses when asked to bear one another's burdens.","anchor":"وحكى الحكم بن أبان عن عكرمة أنه قال بلغني أن اليهودي والنصراني يرى الرجل المسلم يوم القيامة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["35:18"],"words":["إِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ الَّذِينَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُم"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The Prophet warns all people, but the verse singles out those who fear their Lord because they are the ones who benefit from the warning.","anchor":"وهو ينذر الخلق كلهم فخص الذين يخشون ربهم","mentions":[]}]}
